+# GPT-6.2 Sol route preparation
+
+F103 adds explicit `openai/gpt-6.2-sol` selection through the existing OpenAI Responses transport. The source declaration supports text and image input, strict JSON Schema output, caller tools and web search. Existing saved defaults remain unchanged.
+
+The [official model catalogue](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models) lists `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh` and `max` reasoning efforts for this exact model. The [model reference](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6.2-sol) rejects `none` and documents a 1,050,000-token context, 922,000-token input limit and 128,000-token output limit. The route uses `openai_responses_reasoning_tools`, which omits sampling controls. Model discovery records the catalogue registration time as `created`, consistent with the [client contract](client-protocols.md).
+
+## Prices
+
+Standard prices, verified November 21, 2026, are USD per million tokens:
+
+| Input-token count | Input | Output | Cache read |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Through 272,000 | 2 | 10 | 0.10 |
+| Above 272,000 | 4 | 15 | 0.20 |
+
+The [model reference](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6.2-sol) specifies cache-write rates for 30-minute and 12-hour retention. The current catalogue cache classes do not represent either retention period. F103 leaves cache-write price selection unavailable. The Standard rates do not describe Batch, Fast, Ultrafast, discounted background completion windows or negotiated account charges. Local price eligibility starts at `2026-11-21T00:00:00Z`; that time does not claim a provider publication date.
+
+The [image guide](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/images-vision) supplies the request-payload and image-count bounds. The native proxy's smaller encoded-body bound still applies before provider dispatch.
+
+## Validation and activation
+
+Focused public-contract tests cover discovery, medium reasoning with an image and strict schema, token-usage headers, unsupported effort and excessive output rejection, and the 272,000/272,001 price boundary. They use a local provider protocol implementation and establish proxy serialization and admission behavior.
+
+Production activation requires a separately authorized release of the reviewed catalogue state. The current proxy checkout also contains unrelated pending changes; source preparation does not authorize their publication. Read authenticated tenant model discovery after activation, then qualify the exact route through the existing tenant connection before the benchmark arm. Retain the original idempotency key and use ordinary reconciliation for uncertain requests.
+
+No live provider request, tenant change, publication or deployment is part of this preparation. The selected final full CI gate remains with the primary agent after all authorized work and required inputs are complete.
